infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Core Web Vitals: the Good/Poor thresholds, judged at field p75
  desc Aggregate each metric to the field p75 per route per deploy, then judge it against these fixed bands — the rating the beacon reports. The lab Lighthouse run cannot see them; only the field can.
  lists
    - label LCP — Largest Contentful Paint
      desc Good under 2.5 s, poor past 4 s. The bad deploy moved product-page LCP from 2.1 s to 3.4 s — past Good but short of the 4 s poor line, so no lab alarm fired for nine days.
    - label INP — Interaction to Next Paint
      desc Good under 200 ms, poor past 500 ms. Responsiveness lives in the browser, so only a field beacon can report where a route actually sits.
    - label CLS — Cumulative Layout Shift
      desc Good under 0.1, poor past 0.25. A unitless visual-stability score, judged at p75 — strict enough to surface the painful tail without one broken extension paging you.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #8b5cf6
